ARM64EC: Report guest protection boundaries to Wine's memory query.

Write traps split a physically writable code allocation into RX and RWX
regions; adjacent real RX pages can also join the trapped pages. Adjusting
only MEMORY_BASIC_INFORMATION.Protect leaves incorrect RegionSize values.
Expose an optional hook that adjusts protection and clamps the physical
region at the next writable-code or DEP-promotion interval boundary.
Keep the existing nonblocking lock rule and the old scalar export.

Paired with Wine 0047. tests/x64-fidelity/regiontest.c checks every page
before/after execution, then genuine RX and decommit boundaries. M4 control:
78 pass / 82 fail; paired correction 160/0, in normal and full validation.
The x64 Wine control gives 160/0. Native Windows references and FH6 gameplay
remain pending. No JIT code generation changes or cache-format change.

